{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Cherub.</b> Now the cherubim are along the length; therefore the poles are across the width of the Ark. And the critic [Ma'ari] said that צלע is called only along the length, and his proof is ולצלע המשכן השנית (below 26:20), and his answer is בצדו, and חמשה בריחים לקרשי צלע המשכן לירכתים (ibid. 26:27). And from the cover itself they made the cherubim on the two ends of the Ark:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Resolved המערער as 'the critic'; likely refers to Samuel ben Meir (Rashbam), Ibn Ezra's frequent disputant on Exodus."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:19.399946983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}